{"id":"int-0e47ab11191090f953e7fb456c9e2733","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-06-08T14:16:28.057839Z","actor":"Aaron Weegens","issue_id":"bead_chain-dov","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"FALSE POSITIVE / not-a-bug — won't fix. The docs/*.md deletions the build agent observed were INTENTIONAL maintainer edits, not a build-step regression. Decision: FlowDoc-authored docs supersede hand-authored ones, so docs/ is deliberately ceded to the generated FlowDoc HTML site (this is option 3 from the bug's own suggested-fix list). The hand-authored README/getting-started/usage/troubleshooting were removed on purpose; any surviving hand-authored artifacts now live in notes/ (per the docs-vs-notes convention, bead_chain-feu/bch). There is therefore no collision and nothing to recover — do NOT git checkout the deleted files. The FlowDoc-html build (mol-d79/mol-33a) owning docs/ is correct, intended behavior."}}
